@startuml EMREX_2.0_Simple_Flow

title **EMREX v2.0 Simplified Flow**

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

participant "Student" as student
participant "Emrex Client (EMC)" as emc
participant "Foreign Emrex Data Provider (EMP)" as emp
participant "EMREX Registry\n(EMREG)" as emreg

== 1. Select Emrex data provider ==
student -> emc: Logs in to the emrex client
emc -> emreg: Requests list of\navailable Emrex data providers
emreg --> emc: Returns list of Emrex data providers(e.g., )
emc -> student: Shows selection screen
student -> emc: Selects Emrex data provider\n(e.g., "DUO")

== 2. Secure Redirect to Emrex data provider ==
emc -> emp: Redirects student with\nsecure link (OAuth2 + PKCE protected)
note right: Student leaves Emrex client\nand arrives at Emrex data provider

== 3. Login and Select Results ==
student -> emp: Logs in with Emrex data provider
emp -> emp: Verifies student identity
emp -> student: Shows available results\n(courses, grades, diplomas)
student -> emp: Selects results to transfer\n+ gives consent
emp -> emp: Stores selection temporarily

== 4. Return to Emrex client ==
emp -> emc: Redirects student back with\ntemporary access code (valid for 5 minutes)
note left: Access code is short-lived and strictly\nscoped to selected results only

== 5. Fetch and Save Results ==
emc -> emp: Requests results using\naccess code (automatically)
emp --> emc: Sends signed results in selected formats:\n- ELMO XML (optional)\n- ELM JSON (optional)\n- PDF + Metadata (optional)\n- UserInfo (ELMO Learner)\n- EIDAS UserInfo (optional)
note right: Each response is signed so the EMC can verify its authenticity
emc -> emc: Verifies X-Signature with EMP public key\nand saves results to student record
emc -> student: Shows confirmation:\n"Results received successfully!"

@enduml